[00:00.000] 作词 : Wendy Eisenberg
[00:01.000] 作曲 : Wendy Eisenberg
[00:33.864] I wondered when I was younger
[00:38.463] If I would feel this way forever
[00:43.856] Or if this world would finally settle into something solid
[00:53.496]
[00:56.413] I want to be acknowledged
[01:06.884] The fact that the walls were caving in
[01:13.069] Somehow seemed a kind of comfort
[01:22.161] I wanted to feel comfort
[01:27.298]
[01:38.047] Isn't time like an improvisation?
[01:44.963] Like money, sometimes moving
[01:54.602] Meaningless except for how it moves things
[02:07.287]
[02:11.178] Things feel stable, as if they'll continue to feel stable
[02:24.745] I trust that that's a good thing
[02:32.280] Sometimes I'll need convincing
[02:37.742]
[02:52.297] A memory, when I was twelve or thirteen
[02:58.094] I'd write songs close to midnight
[03:02.359] And some of them would sound a bit like this one, even back then
[03:09.842]
[03:14.947] I seem to be consistent
[03:25.657] If rootless in this half-guarded impulse
[03:31.713] I cannot find the walls
[03:37.757]
[04:13.423] I trust that that's a good thing
[04:21.751] Sometimes I'll need convincing
